{"_id":"68dce03b166b018f83df7558","roadmapSlug":"css","nodeId":"eR9zEKc2xQtOPNjOgke4_","description":"# CSS\n\nCSS (Cascading Style Sheets) is a language used to describe the presentation of a document written in HTML or XML, including colors, layout, and fonts. It allows you to separate the content of your website (HTML) from its visual design, making websites more maintainable and adaptable. CSS uses rules to define how elements should be displayed, targeting specific HTML elements or groups of elements.","resources":[{"type":"course","title":"CSS Full Course for Beginners","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=n4R2E7O-Ngo","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144ba"},{"type":"course","title":"HTML & CSS Full Course - Beginner to Pro","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=G3e-cpL7ofc","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144bb"},{"type":"course","title":"Responsive Web Design Certification - Co-Learn HTML & CSS with guided projects","url":"https://www.freecodecamp.org/learn/2022/responsive-web-design/","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144bc"},{"type":"article","title":"Web.dev by Google ΓÇö Learn CSS","url":"https://web.dev/learn/css/","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144bd"},{"type":"feed","title":"Explore top posts about CSS","url":"https://app.daily.dev/tags/css?ref=roadmapsh","_id":"6a67293033d15c83102144be"}],"createdAt":"2025-10-01T08:03:07.533Z","updatedAt":"2026-07-27T09:47:28.129Z","lessonPacks":[{"_id":"6a22adddac1c5fa9928ab3ab","title":"CSS Fundamentals","slug":"css","description":"Style, lay out, and debug real pages without fighting the cascade.","lessonIds":["6a15d62fac1c5fa9928a3fb6","6a15e1b0ac1c5fa9928a403f","6a16f11aac1c5fa9928a7c14","6a19dcdfac1c5fa9928a84a5","6a19e79cac1c5fa9928a8571","6a19f85cac1c5fa9928a8654","6a1d7a23ac1c5fa9928a8b4e","6a1dd2daac1c5fa9928a9884","6a1ecf18ac1c5fa9928a9a81","6a1f3245ac1c5fa9928a9cdd","6a20aa64ac1c5fa9928aa44a","6a20ba69ac1c5fa9928aa755","6a20c105ac1c5fa9928aa818","6a20c2e5ac1c5fa9928aa847","6a20c490ac1c5fa9928aa871","6a20c5adac1c5fa9928aa884","